 "about_text": "JAPAN HOUSE Los Angeles is a cultural institution rather than a commercial gallery, part of a worldwide project with hubs in London, Los Angeles, and São Paulo conceived by Japan's Ministry of Foreign Affairs. Located on two floors of Ovation Hollywood, it includes an exhibition gallery, a WAZA Shop, a library, a multi-purpose event hall (Salon), and a restaurant space. Its programming spans Japanese culture broadly, from traditional crafts and regional artisans to contemporary design, food, film, and music, featuring Japanese artists, chefs, and designers alongside professionals influenced by Japan. The organization began operations in Los Angeles starting in 2016, with the venue's grand opening in 2018.",
